# HotScan India — Environment Variables
#
# These variables are required for the Vercel Edge Function (api/groq.js) that
# proxies requests to the Groq AI API.  Add them in:
#   Vercel dashboard → Project → Settings → Environment Variables
#
# Get free Groq API keys at https://console.groq.com (takes ~2 minutes each).
# At least GROQ_API_KEY_1 is required; additional keys enable round-robin
# rotation so free-tier quota is spread across multiple keys.

GROQ_API_KEY_1=gsk_replace_with_your_key_1
GROQ_API_KEY_2=gsk_replace_with_your_key_2
GROQ_API_KEY_3=gsk_replace_with_your_key_3
GROQ_API_KEY_4=gsk_replace_with_your_key_4
GROQ_API_KEY_5=gsk_replace_with_your_key_5

# Notes
# ─────
# • SUPA_URL and SUPA_KEY in src/config.js are the Supabase *anon* (public)
#   key — intentionally shipped in client code per Supabase design; Row-Level
#   Security ensures each user can only access their own data.
# • RZP_KEY in src/config.js is the Razorpay *publishable* key — a public
#   client-side credential equivalent to Stripe's publishable key.
# • No other secrets are needed to run the app locally or in production.
